# PON: Memory management ON - 16-bit mask instruction
# YAML: mask "1111_1111_1111_1111", opcode "150410" (octal)
# Requires: Proper system state setup
#
# Enables the memory management system by setting the PONI flag in status register.
# On ND-100 this is bit 14 of the STS register.
# Next instruction will use pageindex table specified by PCR.
#
# Prerequisites:
# - Interrupt system enabled (IONI = 1)
# - Internal hardware interrupts enabled
# - Page tables and PCR registers initialized
#
# P-code implementation:
# STS[14,14] = 1;  # Set PONI (Memory management ON) flag
#
# SLEIGH Limitation: Cannot implement due to 16-bit mask
# Manual implementation would be:
# :PON {
#     STS[14,14] = 1;  # Enable memory management
#     # Enter protected mode with hardware memory protection
# }